                <pb facs="1026" n="998" xml:id="pg998"/>

                <head>Enclosure III</head>
                <p rendition="#center">RESEARCH AND REPORTS</p>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">Problem:</hi> To Implement NSC 50 with
                    Respect to the Responsibility for Research and Reports.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Discussion:</hi>
                </p>
                <p>1. The NSC 50 states that in CIA there has been a confusion between national
                    intelligence and miscellaneous research and reporting, and that while NSCID’s on
                    this subject are sound, they have not been effectively carried out (para. 5a).
                    It also states that out of the present ORE there should be created (a) a small
                    Estimates Division which would draw upon and review the specialized intelligence
                    product of the interdepartmental agencies in order to prepare coordinated
                    national intelligence estimates, and (b) a Research and Reports Division to
                    accomplish research in and coordinate production of intelligence in recognized
                    fields of common interest.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Recommendation:</hi>
                    <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>That, aside from national intelligence, CIA will produce intelligence
                            reports only in fields of common concern, as prescribed by the DCI on
                            the advice of the IAC.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>That, on a priority basis, ICAPS prepare for consideration in IAC
                            recommendations on the delineations of fields of common concern.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
            </div>
